metro police say a child was thrown from  a third floor balcony in the southeast  part of town the person responsible  police say is now behind bars this  happened at the boulder pines apartment  complex on boulder highway south of  desert inn joe moeller joins us with  more on what people in the area are  saying  we are still waiting on an update on how  that child is doing this evening many  are still wondering what sparked a  person to throw a child from a third  story at this apartment complex when  police arrived they found the  five-year-old and a male who had been  shot both were transported to the  hospital we were told the adult male was  shot by a member of the child's family  during a struggle after the child was  thrown we spoke to tony hennessey who  lives nearby sickening  it don't make any sense why you would do  that to a child  even in a family dispute  why involve the children a man who lives  in the complex said yesterday he  witnessed an adult being taken into  custody that person also expressed  concern with the complex and the need  for more security we'll update you as  soon as more details become available  joe mohler 8 news now
 

